settings: vManage returns retrieveInterval as a NUMBER, and the model refuses it

The enterprise-CA onboarding step dies READING vManage's current certificate
settings, not writing them:

  TASK [Switch certificate signing to the enterprise CA]
  fatal: [vmanage -> localhost]: FAILED! => {"changed": false,
    "msg": "Task failed: Module failed: 1 validation error for Certificate
            retrieveInterval
              Input should be a valid string
              [type=string_type, input_value=1, input_type=int]"}

The module sends a payload of one field -- Certificate(certificate_signing=...)
-- and never passes retrieve_interval at all (administration_settings.py:354).
The failure is on the NEXT call, get_certificates, whose response the SDK
validates into this same model. vManage 20.18.4 serialises retrieveInterval as a
JSON number; the model declares Optional[str]; pydantic refuses it.

So the appliance is not misbehaving and neither is our task. The SDK's model is
stricter than the API it models, and nothing on our side can pass a value that
avoids it, because the offending value is the DEVICE'S.

coerce_numbers_to_str is pydantic's own answer to exactly this. It is set on the
model rather than the field, so validity_period gets the same tolerance -- it is
declared Optional[str] beside retrieve_interval and there is no reason to think
a device that returns one as a number will not return the other. Only
retrieveInterval is MEASURED; the widening is deliberate and named here.

Applied to the pip-installed SDK (catalystwan==0.41.5.dev2) rather than fixed at
source, because the SDK is a dependency and not a vendored fork. The pin stays:
stable 0.41.x dropped the Enterprise Root CA implementation this lane depends on
(docs/COMPATIBILITY.md).

NOTE ON FORMAT: no "-- / 2.51.0" git trailer. This series is applied with
patch(1) rather than `git apply`, because its target is a pip package in
dist-packages and not a git work tree. patch(1) treats the trailer as a
malformed hunk and refuses the whole file.

--- a/catalystwan/endpoints/configuration_settings.py
+++ b/catalystwan/endpoints/configuration_settings.py
@@ -50,4 +50,4 @@
 class Certificate(BaseModel):
-    model_config = ConfigDict(populate_by_name=True)
+    model_config = ConfigDict(populate_by_name=True, coerce_numbers_to_str=True)
     certificate_signing: str = Field(serialization_alias="certificateSigning", validation_alias="certificateSigning")
     validity_period: Optional[str] = Field(
